# Teach the why

The user is reviewing `services/web` React and will ask questions. **Lead with the design reason**, then the code.

Typical reasons in this take-home:

- **Money / stock:** server is source of truth (cart body `{ sku, qty }`, checkout empty + `Idempotency-Key`, prices from locked products).
- **Auth is not a button:** hide `/admin` in the SPA; API still 403s a shopper.
- **Responsive:** catalog ~375px (2 columns) and desktop (max 6). Overlay on product cards because hover does not exist on phones.
- **XSS:** `{product.name}` as text, never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.
- **Staff bar:** shared `api` client, debounce 300ms, `q` only if length ≥ 2, loading/empty/error on every screen.

Do not answer only “what the function does”. Say why that shape beat the alternative (localStorage cart, JWT, guest checkout, Pinterest-red clone, etc.).
